WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.870
<v Narrator>So now let's talk about AWS Cloud Map.</v>

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:06.130
So Cloud Map is a fully managed resource discovery service

3
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.410
and just that you know at

4
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.920
from a high level going into the exam.

5
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:10.753
So how does that work?

6
00:00:10.753 --> 00:00:12.600
Well when you don't have Cloud Map

7
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.310
and you have for example two services,

8
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.350
a frontend and a backend service then the backend service

9
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.100
will have a version one of it running and the frontend

10
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.700
is meant to be connecting to that version one.

11
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.590
But the day you are deploying a new version

12
00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.520
of your backend service for example version two

13
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.940
and you want your frontend service to connect to it,

14
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.270
you first need to disconnect it from version one,

15
00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:33.120
operate a code change in your frontend service,

16
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.270
redeploy it and then your frontend service

17
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.610
can be connecting to the version two

18
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.280
of your backend service.

19
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.750
Now this is not really good because there's a lot

20
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.060
of coaches required and manual things happening.

21
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.460
So Cloud Map instead allows you to create a map

22
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.040
of the backend services and resources

23
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.620
that your applications depend on.

24
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.210
And then you can add them with their attributes,

25
00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.710
their location and also register the health status all

26
00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.820
within Cloud Map.

27
00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.020
So with Cloud Map,

28
00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.320
what happens at a frontend service and the backend service

29
00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.910
will also connect through Cloud Map.

30
00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.190
So how does that work?

31
00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.460
Well the frontend service will be performing a request,

32
00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.917
a query on Cloud Map to say,

33
00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:09.910
"Hey where can I find the backend service?"

34
00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.690
And here is the version one of the backend service

35
00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.350
you can find so the frontend service

36
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.870
knows how you connect to the backend service.

37
00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.990
Now when we create a version two of our backend service

38
00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:20.940
what's going to happen is that we are going to do

39
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.430
an API call against Cloud Map to update the end points

40
00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.510
from version one to version two.

41
00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:28.140
And the next time the frontend service we'll do

42
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.960
a look up on Cloud Map.

43
00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.490
Then we'll find the location of the version two

44
00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:33.497
of the backend service

45
00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:36.080
and then we'll be able to connect to version two.

46
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.320
The differences is up here.

47
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.700
We didn't do any code change and all the changes

48
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.300
were registered from within Cloud Map okay?

49
00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.830
So this is really cool.

50
00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.800
It also has integration with health checking

51
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.280
to stop sending traffic to unhealthy endpoints.

52
00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.890
And then your application can use Cloud Map using

53
00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.260
for example the SDK, API or DNS queries because Cloud Map

54
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.997
is tightly integrated with route 53 okay?

55
00:01:57.997 --> 00:02:00.470
So that's it just a high level overview of Cloud Map

56
00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.303
is all you need to know.

57
00:02:01.303 --> 00:02:03.620
Okay it's a way for you to do service discovery.

58
00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:06.570
I hope you liked it and I will see you in the next lecture.

